statement:
Let $\mathcal C$ be a site small in the module universe [def-weil-size-convention, def-weil-pbc-sites-and-cohomology], $\mathcal O$ a sheaf of commutative rings, and $t$ a global section of $\mathcal O$ such that multiplication by $t$ is injective. Use module sheaves and unbounded derived categories [def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category, def-weil-abstract-derived-category]. For $P\in D(\mathcal O)$ choose a K-flat representative $Q$ [def-pc-kflat-complex, lem-pc-kflat-resolution]. Put $B_n=\mathcal O/t^n\mathcal O$ and $K_n=[\mathcal O\xrightarrow{t^n}\mathcal O]$ in degrees $[-1,0]$, with transition $(t,1)$, and let $U_\bullet=(Q\otimes_{\mathcal O} B_n)_n$ and $V_\bullet=(Q\otimes_{\mathcal O}K_n)_n$ be strict towers with their quotient and degree-zero Koszul augmentations [def-pc-tensor-complex-sheaves]. Write $R\lim$ for total right derived inverse limit on strict towers, computed by K-injectives, and $\prod^D$ for the product in $D(\mathcal O)$ [lem-weil-pbc-ringed-strict-tower-homotopy-limit]. Let $\operatorname{comp}_P:P\to R\lim U_\bullet$ and $\kappa_P:P\to C_t(P)=R\lim V_\bullet$ be the canonical maps obtained from these strict augmentations using the derived constant-tower/limit unit [lem-coef-derived-tower-counit-projections].

The quotient chain maps $K_n\to B_n[0]$ give a natural isomorphism $c_P:C_t(P)\xrightarrow{\sim}R\lim U_\bullet$ satisfying $c_P\kappa_P=\operatorname{comp}_P$. The following conditions on $P$ are equivalent:
(i) there exists a distinguished triangle $P\xrightarrow{(q_n)}\prod_n^D U_n\xrightarrow{1-s}\prod_n^D U_n\to P[1]$, with first components the actual quotient reductions and $s$ the transition shift [def-weil-derived-limit];
(ii) $P$ is locally derived $(t)$-complete: for every slice object $W$ and $f\in(t)\mathcal O(W)$, $R\mathcal Hom_{\mathcal O_W}(\mathcal O_W[1/f],P|_W)=0$, where localization is sheafified sectionwise [def-pur-derived-internal-hom];
(iii) the specified $\kappa_P$ is invertible;
(iv) the specified $\operatorname{comp}_P$ is invertible.
These assertions are independent of the K-flat representative. They impose no exactness of countable products of module sheaves, no Noetherian or finite-quotient condition, and no boundedness condition. Condition (i) asserts existence of a triangle; it does not choose its isomorphism to the total limit or identify such a choice with either canonical unit.
